150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 45 0 R
/E (YARN is responsible for cluster resource management. Queue-based allocation and scheduling policies provide a mechanism to control contention and prevent one workload from exhausting shared capacity. The exact percentages and limits should be derived from the organization's workload profile because the assessment does not provide a specific cluster size or user distribution.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 45 0 R
/T (4.5 Conclusion)
/E (4.5 Conclusion)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 45 0 R
/E (The starvation is best addressed by introducing structured queues, fair/capacity-aware scheduling, resource limits, workload prioritization where necessary, and continuous resource monitoring. This changes the cluster from uncontrolled contention to managed resource sharing.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
